---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Buildprint docs"
  description="Developer-first guide to Buildprint packet files, markdown structure, read order, and getting started."
>
  <main class="docs-page" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
    <section class="docs-hero">
      <div class="container docs-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="deck-kicker">Docs</p>
          <h1 id="docs-title">Buildprints are markdown packets agents can run.</h1>
          <p class="deck-lead">A Buildprint is a small folder of markdown and structured files. The markdown explains the work. The YAML routes the agent. The proof files define when the job is actually done.</p>
          <div class="standard-actions">
            <a class="btn primary" href="#getting-started">Get started</a>
            <a class="btn" href="/standard/">Packet standard</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="docs-terminal" aria-label="Basic Buildprint file structure">
          <div class="docs-terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>example-buildprint/</b></div>
          <pre><code>example-buildprint/
|-- BUILDPRINT.md       # start here
|-- README.md           # human overview
|-- blueprint.yaml      # machine-readable route
|-- 00-questions.md     # alignment before code
|-- 01-project-setup.md # repo setup and commands
|-- 02-ui-identity.md   # product/UI rules
|-- 03-phases/
|   |-- phase-index.yaml
|   |-- phase-flow.md
|   |-- 01-contracts.md
|   |-- 02-implementation.md
|   `-- 03-verification.md
`-- HANDOVER.md         # final receipt</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container docs-section">
      <div class="docs-section-head">
        <span>The basic idea</span>
        <h2>Put the work in files before the agent starts coding.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="docs-flow" aria-label="Buildprint workflow">
        <article>
          <b>1</b>
          <h3>Describe the target</h3>
          <p>What should exist when the work is done, and what must not change.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <b>2</b>
          <h3>Order the work</h3>
          <p>Setup first, then contracts, implementation, wiring, and verification.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <b>3</b>
          <h3>Run the proof</h3>
          <p>Tests, fixtures, receipts, or known limits decide whether the job is complete.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container docs-section docs-two-up">
      <div class="docs-section-head">
        <span>Two common shapes</span>
        <h2>Product packets build a system. Capability packets add one reusable power.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="docs-shape-grid">
        <article class="docs-shape">
          <h3>Product Buildprint</h3>
          <p>Use this when the agent is building a whole app, tool, or major product surface.</p>
          <pre><code>product-buildprint/
|-- BUILDPRINT.md
|-- 00-questions.md
|-- 01-project-setup.md
|-- 02-ui-identity.md
|-- blueprint.yaml
|-- 03-phases/
|   |-- phase-index.yaml
|   |-- phase-flow.md
|   `-- 01-...md
`-- HANDOVER.md</code></pre>
        </article>

        <article class="docs-shape">
          <h3>Capability Buildprint</h3>
          <p>Use this when the agent is adding one bounded feature to an existing app, like RBAC or subscriptions.</p>
          <pre><code>capability-buildprint/
|-- BUILDPRINT.md
|-- capability.yaml
|-- compatibility.md
|-- apply.md
|-- verify.md
|-- 00-host-assessment.md
|-- 01-integration-plan.md
`-- 02-implementation-phases/
    |-- 01-contract-and-config.md
    |-- 02-core-integration.md
    |-- 03-host-wiring.md
    `-- 05-verification-and-receipt.md</code></pre>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container docs-section">
      <div class="docs-section-head">
        <span>Read order</span>
        <h2>Tell the agent where authority lives.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="docs-read-order">
        <div class="docs-read-step">
          <b>BUILDPRINT.md</b>
          <p>The canonical start file. It names the goal, read order, phase gates, and acceptance rules.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="docs-read-step">
          <b>Questions and setup</b>
          <p>Alignment, assumptions, environment commands, package manager, and repo constraints.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="docs-read-step">
          <b>Phases</b>
          <p>Small ordered implementation files. Each phase should be clear enough to review.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="docs-read-step">
          <b>Verification</b>
          <p>Required proof before the agent can call the work finished.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="getting-started" class="container docs-section docs-start">
      <div>
        <span>Getting started</span>
        <h2>Use an existing Buildprint first.</h2>
        <p>Pick the closest packet, load exact files, then ask the agent to follow the packet instead of guessing from a loose prompt.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="docs-command-card">
        <p>For an agent-readable bootstrap:</p>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/DomEscobar/agent-buildprint
node agent-buildprint/bin/agb.js start \
  https://agent-buildprint.com/buildprints/rbac-permissions/package.json .

# then read:
.buildprint/next-agent.md</code></pre>
        <p>Manual path: open a Buildprint, read <code>BUILDPRINT.md</code>, answer alignment questions, follow phases, run verification, then write the handover.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
